{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And a man, when he sells.</b> After the verse spoke of the matter of selling a house, the verse returns to give the reason for the matter — how could this thing be, that HaShem sell His patrimony, the chosen House? It is His saying ״וְאִישׁ״ — this is the Holy One, blessed be He; <b>when he sells a house of dwelling</b> — meaning, a house in which is the dwelling of Elohim, this is the Temple; ״עִיר חוֹמָה״ — this is Jerusalem, as it is written (Psalms 122:2) ״יְרוּשָׁלַיִם הָרִים סָבִיב לָהּ״. He said the reason is <b>and its redemption shall be</b> — that through this very thing, on the contrary, it will be redeemed. This is along the lines of what they said, their memory for blessing (Midrash Tehillim 79:1), concerning the verse ״מִזְמוֹר לְאָסָף״ etc., that HaShem cast His wrath upon wood and stone, for otherwise not a survivor or fugitive of Israel would have remained, and if there is no Israel there is no Temple and no Jerusalem. Therefore ״וְהָיְתָה גְּאֻלָּתוֹ״ — the redemption of the people and the redemption of the House, for there is hope and the children shall return to their border."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:21.982858561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}